# The translation files are UTF-16LE with a BOM, because that is the only
# encoding the Win32 profile APIs read as Unicode (loc.cpp). Line-ending
# normalisation corrupts them: a newline is 0D 00 0A 00, whose 0A reads as a
# lone LF, and checkout rewrites it to 0D 00 0D 0A 00 — one byte too many, and
# every code unit after it is misaligned.
#
# Git already infers this from the NUL bytes. Saying it means a later
# `* text=auto` cannot quietly undo it, since an explicit attribute wins over
# auto-detection.
src/DeskTick/lang/*.ini binary
